<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Occupation of Bosnia-Herzegovina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1878">1878</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as occupation and pacification of Bosnia-Herzegovina</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia-herzegovina">Bosnia-Herzegovina</a> was the entry of Austro-Hungarian troops into the Ottoman provinces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzegovina">Herzegovina</a> in 1878, authorised by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-berlin">Congress of Berlin</a>. The army had to overcome armed local resistance during the pacification. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> administered the territory and formally annexed it in 1908, deepening tensions with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>.</p></div>
